\ Mutation, mutable-container construction and access, a runtime-depth indexed
\ drop, and a value-producing dynamic-variable binding all compile fallback-free
\ under interpreter-free AOT with the interpreter setting locked off. Each
\ construct previously emitted a fallback the zero-fallback class rejects, or
\ relied on a body the interpreter would run: container natives routed through
\ `jitNativeWordCall`, `drop-at`'s runtime-depth `<rot-n` routed through it too,
\ and `with-parameter`'s body had to be compiled to a code pointer rather than
\ executed by the interpreter. A clean build and a run that exits without
\ output prove all of them carry no fallback of any kind. Results are dropped
\ rather than printed because polymorphic display words would themselves emit
\ fallbacks; correctness is checked separately under runtime-image AOT.
M{ } "k" 1 @set! "k" @get drop
V{ 10 20 30 } drop
H{ } "key" 2 @set "key" @get drop

\ `drop-at` indexes the stack at a depth supplied at runtime, so its `<rot-n`
\ has no literal depth to fold and compiles as a direct native call.
1 2 3 4 2 drop-at drop drop drop

\ A value-producing `with-parameter` body compiles to a code pointer; the
\ binding is exercised and its result dropped.
wp: parameter{ [ 0 ] } ;
99 wp [ wp get ] with-parameter drop
